After 51 tries at playing Slash'em, it looked like I finally had a
character that was doing well.  I was amazed as my doppleganger monk
passed level after level without dying, especially since my previous
best character didn't even make it to the quest.  I made it all the
way to the Astral Plane, and was heading towards the first altar.  I
had an AC of -53 and over 500 hit points, so I figured I was
unstoppable.  The altar was 3 squares away and I was surrounded by
monsters on all sides when I received this message:

The invisible Archon casts a spell at you!
A pool appears beneath you!
You fall into the water!
You sink like a rock.
You attempt a teleport spell.
The attempted teleport spell fails.
You drown.

Huh?  An Archon was able to create a pool of water under my feet to
drown me?  I was sorely disappointed by this suprise. :(

I realized too late that I should have teleported monsters away from
me so that I didn't get surrounded.  I also could have used my
doppleganger's liquid leap technique to jump to safety, or I could
have been levitating the whole time.

Is this a Slash'em-only thing, or can this happen in Nethack too?  Are
there any other suprises I should be aware of on Slash'em's Astral
Plane so I can avoid YASD next time?

